---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const { lang = "en" } = Astro.props;
---

<Layout
    title="About SaveTikFast"
    description="Learn how SaveTikFast works, our editorial focus, and our commitment to privacy and respectful use of public content."
    lang={lang}
>
    <section class="page-header">
        <div class="container"><h1>About SaveTikFast</h1></div>
    </section>

    <main class="content-section">
        <article class="text-content">
            <p class="intro">SaveTikFast is an independent web utility and learning resource for people who want to organise references from public TikTok links. We build practical guides for creators and everyday users alongside tools that run in the browser.</p>

            <h2>What we do</h2>
            <p>Our service processes a public link supplied by a visitor and returns available formats for that request. We do not ask visitors to create an account to use the core tool. The format and quality available for a link can depend on the source material, the device, and changes made by the original platform.</p>

            <h2>Respect for creators and rights holders</h2>
            <p>SaveTikFast is designed for material a visitor owns or is authorised to save. A public link does not itself grant permission to copy, republish, sell, or use someone else’s work commercially. Visitors are responsible for checking the creator’s permission, the platform rules, and the law that applies where they live.</p>
            <p>We do not claim ownership of third-party videos, audio, images, trademarks, or accounts. We also provide a <a href="/dmca">DMCA process</a> for rights holders who need to report a concern.</p>

            <h2>Privacy and security</h2>
            <p>We aim to collect only the information needed to operate and protect the service. A link entered into the tool is processed for the requested action; it is not a public post or a user profile. Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains the information we process, the third-party services we use, and the choices available to visitors.</p>

            <h2>Our editorial approach</h2>
            <p>Our articles focus on practical topics such as creator permissions, content planning, accessibility, and responsible digital workflows. Each article is intended to answer a specific question with clear steps, examples, and limitations. We correct or retire information that is no longer useful, and we avoid presenting opinions, estimates, or platform features as guarantees.</p>

            <h2>Contact and feedback</h2>
            <p>Questions, correction requests, and product feedback are welcome at <a href="mailto:support@savetik-fast.xyz">support@savetik-fast.xyz</a>. For copyright notices, please include the relevant public URL and a description of the rights you hold so that we can review the request efficiently.</p>
        </article>
    </main>
</Layout>

<style>
    .page-header { background: var(--surface); padding: 4rem 0; text-align: center; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .page-header h1 { font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 800; margin: 0; }
    .content-section { padding: 4rem 20px; }
    .text-content { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-main); }
    .intro { font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--text-dim); }
    h2 { font-size: 1.7rem; margin: 2.4rem 0 1rem; color: var(--secondary); }
    p { margin: 0 0 1.35rem; }
    a { color: var(--secondary); }
</style>
